### =====================================================================
### END-TO-END (Phase 3): vendor and customer onboarding through events
###
### Everything goes through the API gateway (port 8080).
### Needs: infrastructure, auth-service, customer-service, store-service, api-gateway,
###        and the Debezium connectors (scripts\register-connectors.ps1).
###
### Written for the VS Code "REST Client" extension. Run the requests IN ORDER.
### Steps marked "wait" depend on an event: Kafka delivers it within a second or two.
###
### What it shows:
###   A. vendor3 registers a store -> admin approves it -> StoreApproved event
###      -> auth-service links the store -> vendor3's NEW token contains storeId
###   B. a new customer registers -> UserRegistered event
###      -> customer-service creates the profile -> the customer adds an address
### =====================================================================

@gatewayUrl = http://localhost:8080

@vendorToken = {{vendorLogin.response.body.$.data.accessToken}}
@adminToken = {{adminLogin.response.body.$.data.accessToken}}
@newVendorToken = {{vendorLoginAgain.response.body.$.data.accessToken}}
@newCustomerToken = {{customerRegistration.response.body.$.data.accessToken}}
@newStoreId = {{storeRegistration.response.body.$.data.id}}


### 1. A. vendor3 logs in - the token has NO storeId yet (data.user.storeId = null)
# @name vendorLogin
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "vendor3@grocery.com",
  "password": "Password@123"
}


### 2. A. vendor3 registers a store -> PENDING_APPROVAL (StoreRegistered event)
# @name storeRegistration
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/vendor/store
Authorization: Bearer {{vendorToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Daily Needs Supermarket",
  "description": "Groceries, dairy and household items",
  "phone": "9000000010",
  "addressLine1": "22, 5th Cross, Malleshwaram",
  "city": "Bengaluru",
  "state": "Karnataka",
  "pincode": "560003"
}


### 3. A. Customers cannot see the store yet -> 404
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/stores/{{newStoreId}}


### 4. A. The admin logs in
# @name adminLogin
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@grocery.com",
  "password": "Password@123"
}


### 5. A. The admin approves the store -> ACTIVE (StoreApproved event)
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/admin/stores/{{newStoreId}}/approve
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}


### 6. A. (wait a moment) vendor3 logs in again -> data.user.storeId is now the new store id
# @wait 3
# @name vendorLoginAgain
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "vendor3@grocery.com",
  "password": "Password@123"
}


### 7. A. The store is now visible to everyone, without a token
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/stores/{{newStoreId}}


### 8. A. vendor3 manages the store with the new token
PATCH {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/vendor/store/accepting-orders
Authorization: Bearer {{newVendorToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "acceptingOrders": true
}


### 9. B. A new customer registers (UserRegistered event)
# @name customerRegistration
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Kavya Nair",
  "email": "kavya.nair@example.com",
  "phone": "9123412340",
  "password": "Password@123",
  "role": "CUSTOMER"
}


### 10. B. (wait a moment) Her customer profile was created from the event
# @wait 3
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/customers/me
Authorization: Bearer {{newCustomerToken}}


### 11. B. She adds her first address -> automatically the default
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/customers/me/addresses
Authorization: Bearer {{newCustomerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "label": "HOME",
  "contactName": "Kavya Nair",
  "contactPhone": "9123412340",
  "addressLine1": "11, 3rd Main, Malleshwaram",
  "city": "Bengaluru",
  "state": "Karnataka",
  "pincode": "560003"
}


### 12. B. Which stores deliver to her PIN code? (the new store does)
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/stores?pincode=560003
